  "title": "Ember Shelter",
  "rules": [
    "Three foragers share a timber shelter and a clay kiln; each pack holds only three material units.",
    "Build with timber and insulate with kiln lining. Both wall and lining must reach two for shared night protection.",
    "The kiln consumes one timber and one clay, finishes after three transitions, and releases smoke.",
    "A timber-fed hearth adds four shared heat. Night protection needs enough heat for the current cold severity.",
    "Day lasts 12 ticks and night six; the third sunrise ends the expedition at tick 54.",
    "At night, unprotected workers lose health. Shelter protection reaches Manhattan distance two from its footprint.",
    "Night end wears one wall level. Thick kiln smoke hurts nearby workers and can wear walls.",
    "Pass materials to adjacent workers or put your private preferred material into the locker for a personal bonus.",
    "Use actual wall, lining, heat, smoke and weather state to depict a timber-block refuge, warm hearth and cold forest clearing."
  ],
